# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the sanitizer CI job. Read through
# LSAN_OPTIONS, not ASAN_OPTIONS: ASan's own suppression parser rejects the
# leak: type and aborts the process.
#
# rosidl's C++ type support registers its message descriptors in static storage
# that is never torn down, and bringing up any rclcpp node reaches it through
# rcl_node_init. The allocations are one-time and process-lifetime rather than
# per-node: the reported total is byte-identical in a 24-test binary and an
# 87-test one, and no prox_mpc frame appears in any of the leak stacks. The
# controller fixtures already call on_cleanup() and then reset(), so there is no
# teardown to add.
#
# Scoped deliberately to those two frames: detect_leaks stays on (see
# ASAN_OPTIONS in .github/workflows/ci.yaml), so a leak in this repository's own
# allocations still fails the job.
#
# print_suppressions=1 reports the hit count per entry, which is how a stale
# entry here is told apart from one that is still doing work.
leak:librosidl_typesupport_cpp
leak:rcl_node_init
